pages.free_user:
Logging is Premium in the iPhone app, so a free user usually has nothing logged. The card then shows only:
- the title, the seven letters and the dashes for past days;
- no bars, no figures and no target line, and never sample or decorative bars (rule 1);
- one sentence: "Each day's calories show here once you log your meals."

There is no button: the existing free card under the dots is the one offer. The sentence doesn't name Pro or Premium, so it doesn't wait on that decision.

A free user who has real entries this week (for example after a trial) sees them exactly as a Premium user does: showing what's there is never gated. On numbite.com nothing is gated, so everyone gets the full page.

build_list:
Tests first, in a new web/tests/week.test.ts for lib/mm/week.ts. weekDays(log, now) gives 7 days, each with: state past/today/future, calories, the protein sum and count, entries, protein gaps and estimates. Cases:
- a day with nothing logged is not 0 and is not counted;
- today is left out of the averages;
- Monday, and a week where only today is logged;
- a calories-only entry adds no protein and counts as a gap, and a day with no protein figure at all is left out of protein's day count;
- portion-scaled entries;
- entries at 23:59 and 00:01 land on the right local day;
- entries after today are ignored;
- the scale top = max(target, highest day) x 1.15;
- lastWeekAverage shows only when last week has logged days.

Tests first, in a new web/tests/labelTotals.test.ts for lib/mm/labelTotals.ts todayLabelTotals(log, now). Cases:
- the sum and count for each of sugar, salt and fiber;
- n counts every entry today, typed and estimate entries included;
- k = 0 reads as "not published";
- a bad stored value (NaN, a negative number, a string) is skipped and not counted in k;
- sodium is never turned into salt;
- only today's entries count.

Tests first for the stores and sanitizers:
- sanitizeLog keeps estimate only when it is exactly true and drops anything else;
- homePagesStore's sanitizer keeps { seen, slid, hintDays, lastHintDay } and resets anything malformed;
- the hint shows only while seen is false and hintDays is under 5, and a new day adds 1 to hintDays, a repeat visit on the same day doesn't.

New e2e/homepages.mjs, run in Chromium (the only Playwright browser installed; gesture checks in WebKit are done in the Simulator and on the iPhone). It checks:
- the three dots are 44x44, and tapping each sets aria-current and brings that page into view;
- the hint shows, takes you to page 2 and goes away for good, and homePagesStore.seen is set;
- the hint is gone on a 6th day without page 2 being seen (fake the clock);
- page 1 is still in view after a reload;
- with reduced motion there is no transform, and dot scrolling is instant;
- the slide does not play while Pip's Home tips are due;
- in Arabic the dots follow the page;
- at 320pt the pages stack and the dots are hidden;
- the free user sees empty frames with no bars and no figures;
- a seeded week shows the right figures, dashes and hidden "–", the gap and estimate notes appear, and the Monday wording shows;
- all three pages are in the accessibility tree;
- there is no horizontal page overflow at 360 and 390px or at Extra large text.

